    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the undisputed anchor of the lineup. With a dominant score of 83.29, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a prime #3 hole projection and a highly favorable matchup against Bryce Elder (4.33 xERA), with dynamic platoon advantages pushing his ceiling toward elite territory. We also see high-leverage potential from **Drake Baldwin** (72.67), whose value is bolstered significantly by a 16% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Brandon Young. **Heliot Ramos** (67.32) remains a critical start; while he faces a decent arm in Ryan Johnson, the wind blowing out at the stadium provides a tangible boost, and his elite sprint speed makes him an essential weapon in our pursuit of stolen bases.\n\nOur bench strategy centers on the tight margin between **Dominic Smith** and **Curtis Mead**. While **Curtis Mead** logged a respectable 57.04 score\u2014bolstered by a favorable matchup against Bratt\u2014he ultimately fell short of the starting nine. The optimizer prioritized **Dominic Smith** (62.31) due to the substantial 16% park adjustment he receives, which creates a higher efficiency floor than **Curtis Mead** can currently offer. It is worth noting that we are heavily reliant on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions for players like **Jacob Wilson**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Cole Carrigg**; should any of these players move down in their respective batting orders, their efficiency scores will likely see a downward correction. **Jackson Merrill** also warrants close monitoring; while he carries a solid 59.99, he faces the toughest opposing pitcher of the day in Eu P\u00e9rez (3.78 xERA), making him a high-risk, high-reward play despite the potential for stolen base opportunities.",
